gets small --workers 4` (1 s), `--stage floor --targets gap338 --workers","+8` (22 min wall), `--stage ceiling --targets gap338 --seed 2 --budget-scale 3","+--tag s2x3` then the same with `--targets cs200`, `--stage tables`;","+`nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/obstruction_search/02_expansion/run_harness.py --workers 8`.","+Size range: ceiling 9–134 customers (every corpus target; `open24` is item","+07's); exact `n ≤ 22`; floor the 35 instances of the 338 item 01 censored","+(100–125 customers). Units: optimum units throughout; the ceiling is not a","+bound.*","+","+### 2.1 What was done","+","+**The object and the direction.** For the MOSP graph of an instance,","+`f(t) = min_{|C| = t} |N[C]|`. Harper's bound is `pw ≥ f(t) − t` at every `t`","+(`exists_closedNbhd_card_le`), so family E's bound in optimum units is","+`max_t (f(t) − t) + 1`; the empty-pair bound `n − 2 s* − 2 ≤ pw`","+(`card_sub_two_mul_emptyPairIndex_sub_two_le_pathwidth`) is the same profile","+read through `s* = max_t min(t − 1, n − f(t))`. `satisfiability/expansion_bound.py`'s","+`max_i (i − M(i))` with `M(i) = max{t : f(t) ≤ i}` is the same number as","+`max_t (f(t) − t)` (take `i = f(t) − 1` one way and `t = M(i) + 1` the","+other), so item 01's `harper12` *is* this family's floor at cap 12. A set","+`C` of size `t` found by any search proves `f(t) ≤ |N[C]|` and nothing else;","+the search's value `max_t (f̂(t) − t) + 1`, `f̂ ≥ f`, is a **ceiling**: if it","+is below the optimum, no computation of this family can close the instance.","+","+**The search** (plan §0.5 (c)). Per level `t = 1 … n − 1`, tabu search on","+swaps minimising `|N[C]|` over `|C| = t`, on bit masks in C: cover","+multiplicities per vertex, a shortlist of six entering vertices by gain and","+six leaving by loss, the best of the 36 exact swap deltas applied (tenure","+7 ± 2 on both moved vertices, aspiration on the global best), at most","+2,000 swaps and a stall limit per restart (40 non-improving swaps in the","+sweep, 1