10 over all targets.","+","+**The search against the witness.** The witness's own prefixes give a","+ceiling at the optimum on 4,577 of 4,697 and below it on 120; the search","+lowers the witness's value at 79% of the levels at 101–134 customers (14% at","+9–20) and lowers the *ceiling* below the witness's on 1,519 instances. So","+the planner's third risk (§0.8: \"the ceiling is the optimum almost","+everywhere\") did not materialise: the search finds sets the witness does","+not, and the ceiling is strictly informative on a third of the targets and","+on 95% of the 338.","+","+**The second pass** (`s2x3`: seed 2, budget ×3, 436 instances of","+`gap338 ∪ cs200`, 0.13 core-hours): the ceiling is equal on 432, lower on 1","+(`HS problem 1195`, 13 → 12) and higher on 3 (`HS problem 1181`,","+`Random-100-50-10-4_0`, `Random-100-50-6-3_0`, each by one). The ceiling is","+therefore a search artefact at the ±1 level on about 1% of the instances at","+30–100 customers; the minimum of the two passes is below the optimum on 365","+of the 436 (pass 1 alone: 364). Both passes are valid ceilings; the tables","+quote pass 1.","+","+**Exact at `n ≤ 22`** (4,123 instances, 0.4 ms median each). The search","+attains `f(t)` at every `t` on **4,090 of 4,123 (99.2%)**; the 33 misses","+are one level each, by exactly one vertex, 31 of them at `n = 20` and 2 at","+`n = 15`, and none at an argmax level: the ceiling equals the exact bound","+on **4,123 of 4,123**. Harper exact equals the optimum on **2,933 (71.1%)**:","+78% at `n = 10`, 75% at 15, 59% at 20; the empty-pair value equals the","+optimum on 748 (18.1%) and is never above the Harper value (it is a","+weakening of the same profile: strictly below on 3,473 of the 4,697","+targets, equal on 1,224). Against the record: the exact bound exceeds","+`harper12` on one instance (`scoop-B_18CR1_33_0`, `n = 19`, optimum 4,","+where `expansion_bound` reports 0 for \"no level improves\" and the exact","+value is 1 — a convention, not a bound) and exceeds `lb_best` and `floor0`","+on **none**: at these sizes the full-depth expansion family adds nothing to","+what is on record.","+","+**The floor rerun** (35 instances, `tables.md` (e)). The floor rose on 32 of","+35, by 1.9 stacks on average and by up to **6** (`Random-125-125-6-4_0`","+63 → 69, `6-3_0` 64 → 70, `8-5_0` 83 → 88 — all still 5–11 below the","+optimum); it is **above `floor0`, the best floor on record, on 17 of the","+35** (every density-6 and density-8 125 × 125 instance, `4-1_0`, `4-3_0`,","+`100-100-4-2_0`, …): the cap-12 branch and bound at ten minutes is a new","+record floor there. The bracket closes on 2 (`125-125-10-2_0`, floor =","+ceiling = 103 against 104: the family's duality gap is exactly 1 and it can","+never close the instance; `125-125-10-5_0`, floor = ceiling = optimum = 99)","+and the floor equals the optimum on 1. On the ridge classes it buys one","+stack from a floor of 6–8 against optima of 20–25 (`125-125-2`), and there","+the minor certificates on record (`floor0` 20–24) are the whole story.","+Nine of the 35 did not complete cap 12 in 600 s (every `125-125-2` but","+`2-1_0`, `4-3_0`, `6-1_0`, `6-4_0`, `6-5_0`, `8-5_0`); their values are","+valid at the cap reached.","+","+### 2.3 Through the harness","+","+HARNESS_PLACEHOLDER","+","+### 2.4 Kill verdict and compute","+","+**Kill criterion (plan §0.9, E-search): not met.** The search attains","+`f(t)` at every `t` on 99.2% of the instances at `n ≤ 22`, against the","+criterion's 90%; the ceiling is not search-limited there and equals the","+exact bound on every one. Above 22 the second pass moves it by ±1 on 1% of","+the instances. Item 03 can seed its SAT calls from the search's sets and,","+where they exist, from the exact minimisers (`sets/<name>.json`, keys","+`sets` and `exact_sets`). The two bug conditions — a ceiling below the","+floor, a floor above the optimum — occurred on **0** instances.","+","+**Compute.** Ceiling 0.14, exact 0.00, floor 2.83, second pass 0.13 and the","+harness run (§2.3) core-hours, against the item's 3: the floor's ten-minute","+cap was halved where only one level was missing, and the item still ran","+over because the harness's 10 s per instance on 6,376 instances is a","+validity run the acceptance criteria require.","+","+### 2.5 What this does not claim","+","+That the ceiling is attained by any computation (a ceiling is an upper","+estimate of what the family can prove; the family's true value sits in","+`[floor, ceiling]`); that the floor is the family's best (the exact half","+above cap 12 is item 03); that the search's `f̂` equals `f` above 22","+customers (measured only to 22; the second pass's ±1 says it does not","+always); that any of this changes a solver (no candidate reaches","+`_lower_bound`); that the 17 new record floors are anything but the cap-12","+bound given more time. The closing-layout correction is a statement about","+our construction of seeds, not about Yanasse's equivalence. \"We found no","+prior report\" of a searched vertex-isoperimetric ceiling on benchmark","+instances; the bound itself is Harper (1966)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/obstruction_search.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016bRnZvPsQm6s9xrcTwtej8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
